# The port's half of the kaon+ like-for-like; its partner is kaon_emonly.mac.
#
# MEASURED, 2,000 events (the kaon's dose per event is twice the pion's, so the same relative
# uncertainty comes at a tenth the count):
#
#   kaon+  port 4.91817 +/- 0.0829 nGy   Geant4 4.9184 +/- 0.0817   -0.005%, 0.002 sigma
#
# Agreement to five parts in a hundred thousand, which at this count is luck as much as
# physics - the honest statement is "well inside one combined sigma". What it establishes is
# that the Bragg / Bethe-Bloch chain and the range table generalise to a mass and a lifetime
# nothing in this project had transported before.
#
# RE-MEASURED AT 500,000 events, when the negative kaon was added beside it:
#
#   kaon+  port 1242.97 +/- 1.306 nGy   Geant4 1240.74 +/- 1.302   +0.18%, 1.21 sigma
#
# The 0.005% at 2,000 events was indeed luck; 0.18% at 1.21 sigma is the real size of the
# agreement, and it is still agreement. The negative kaon at the same count is +9.52% at
# 61 sigma - kaon_minus_port.mac and docs/RISK.md.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/gun/particle kaon+
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 500
/run/beamOn 2000
